@startuml 04-orchestration-and-gates
' The DAG, where each quality gate sits, and what each one protects.
' NOTE on the two syntax traps here, both of which fail quietly rather than loudly:
'   1. Colour goes in a stereotype AFTER the ';'  --  :label; <<#FBEAEA>>
'      The older `#FBEAEA:label;` form is rejected inside a partition by
'      PlantUML 1.2026+, and the parse error is reported against the partition's
'      closing brace rather than the offending line.
'   2. Keep each activity label on one source line, using \n escapes.
'      A real line break inside a coloured activity renders a deprecation
'      banner into the image itself.
' Render: make diagrams

title Orchestration — where each gate sits, and what it protects

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #6B7C8F
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #B4553F
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FBEAEA
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF3D6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #C8A96A

start

:<b>preflight</b>\nverify the platform is deployable-into;
note right
  Fails in seconds with a clear message,
  instead of 20 minutes later inside dbt
  with "table does not exist" — which
  reads like a modelling bug.
end note

partition "ingest" {
  :simulate_arrivals;
  :<b>wait_for_files</b>\nsensor · SLA 45 min · retries 0;
  note right
    A sensor already retries by definition.
    Its SLA fires while it is still running
    and still <i>correct</i> — the only mechanism
    that can say "this wait has become abnormal".
  end note
  :load_files\nPUT + COPY;
  :drain_stream\nsingle transaction;

  if (<b>GATE 1 — load integrity</b>\nstuck batch? parse errors > 5%?) then (fail)
    :<b>STOP</b>\nIngestion lost rows.\nRAW is intact — nothing published.; <<#FBEAEA>>
    stop
  else (pass)
  endif
}

partition "transform" {
  :dbt source freshness;
  if (<b>GATE 2 — source freshness</b>\nqueue older than its SLA?) then (error)
    :<b>STOP</b>\nAsked to transform data\nthat never arrived.; <<#FBEAEA>>
    stop
  else (ok / warn)
  endif

  :dbt_seed\nreference data;
  :dbt_run_staging;
  :<b>dbt_run_adjudication</b>\n19 rules · SLA 20 min;

  if (<b>GATE 3 — reject rate</b>\n>= 50 events and rate > 25%?) then (fail)
    :<b>STOP</b>\nRules have run, so the rate is measurable\nand every rejection is already logged —\nbut <b>FCT_TRADE is untouched</b>.\nThe golden record still holds\nthe last known-good state.; <<#FBEAEA>>
    stop
  else (pass)
  endif

  :dbt_run_marts\nSLA 25 min;
  :dbt_test\n162 generic + 6 singular · --store-failures;
  :<b>dbt_snapshot</b>;
  note right
    Snapshot runs <b>after</b> the tests.
    Historising data that just failed its
    tests writes a bad state into immutable
    history, and SCD2 cannot be tidied up
    without destroying the audit trail
    that is its whole purpose.
  end note
}

partition "verify" {
  :<b>reconcile</b>\nmanifest ground truth vs actual verdicts;
  note right
    The only check that can detect an event
    that is <b>absent</b>. Everything else
    validates rows that are present.

    MISSING_EVENT = silent data loss = P1.
  end note

  if (<b>GATE 4 — publish readiness</b>\noverdue expiry? scorecard RED?) then (fail)
    :<b>STOP</b>\nPlatform not fit to publish.; <<#FBEAEA>>
    stop
  else (pass)
  endif

  :report_health;
}

stop

legend left
  <b>DAG settings are correctness, not tuning</b>

  max_active_runs = 1
    Two runs would race on the version
    high-water mark.

  catchup = False
    Rules evaluate against <i>current</i> state.
    Replaying last Tuesday would re-adjudicate
    today's data with last Tuesday's business
    date. Reprocessing is a deliberate,
    separate, logged operation.

  <b>Every gate warns before it blocks.</b>
  Gate 3 warns at 60% of its threshold.
  A control with one setting is either too
  tight and gets disabled, or too loose and
  never fires.

  <b>Overrides are environment variables</b>,
  so an operator's decision to proceed is
  explicit and temporary — not a code change.
endlegend

@enduml
